.TH btctax-income-import 1  btctax "btctax manual"
.SH NAME
import \- Import full\-return inputs from an offline TOML file into the vault for a tax year
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBimport\fR <\fB\-\-year\fR> <\fB\-\-file\fR> [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Import full\-return inputs from an offline TOML file into the vault for a tax year.
.PP
From TY2026 (a Form 1099\-DA basis\-reporting year) the file also carries the broker\-reporting answers: one table per exchange provider, one slot per cohort — `[broker_reporting.coinbase]` with `covered = "basis_matches"` and `noncovered = "not_reported"` (an answer is one of `not_reported`, `proceeds_only`, `basis_matches`, `basis_differs`, `mixed`). `report \-\-tax\-year` lists the keys the ledger needs answered and the rows under each; an answer stored for a key no row carries is refused as unread, and a missing one refuses the return until given. Earlier years neither ask nor accept them.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-year\fR \fI<YEAR>\fR
The tax year (e.g. 2024)
.TP
\fB\-\-file\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Path to the TOML file describing the full\-return inputs
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Load a file that carries the btctax SCRUB marker (a scrubbed copy: synthetic identity, no IP PIN). Without this, importing one is refused — it would overwrite this vault\*(Aqs real identity with placeholders, unrecoverably. Prefer a scratch vault.

This overrides the scrub\-marker guard and NOTHING else; a parked full return still blocks the write.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
